--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evaluation code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The official benchmark checkers are not vendored in this repository. `python -m eval.external.fetch` downloads them
at pinned commits into eval/third_party/ (not tracked by git) and checks every file against the sha256 listed in
eval/external/PINS.json:

  - LiveCodeBench (https://github.com/LiveCodeBench/LiveCodeBench) @ 28fef95, MIT License,
    Copyright (c) 2024 LiveCodeBench
  - IFEval, from google-research (https://github.com/google-research/google-research) @ b24f2136, Apache-2.0,
    Copyright The Google Research Authors
  - IFBench (https://github.com/allenai/IFBench) @ 1091c4c3, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2025 Allen Institute for AI
  - nltk_data (https://github.com/nltk/nltk_data) @ 550b662, the data packages the IF checkers load; each package
    keeps its own license

Two small pieces of eval/ are adapted from third-party code and keep its license:

  - eval/graders/math_grader.py: last_boxed_only_string and remove_boxed are taken verbatim from the G-OPD
    evaluation script (https://github.com/RUCBM/G-OPD, math_eval/eval_math.py), MIT License,
    Copyright (c) 2026 RUCBM.
  - eval/graders/lcb_runtime.py: check_correctness is a modified version of the function of the same name in
    LiveCodeBench's lcb_runner (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 LiveCodeBench); it adds a memory limit and complete
    timeout metadata, and calls the fetched official test runner unchanged.
